Package: vtpm-mds
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: swtpm
Provides: prox-mds, qemu-mds
Conflicts: prox-mds
Replaces: prox-mds
Description: QEMU/Proxmox IMDS and TPM attestation service
 vtpm-mds provides an EC2-IMDSv2-compatible metadata service and
 TPM-anchored workload identity for QEMU guests (Proxmox VE is a
 first-class inventory backend).
 .
 The daemon listens on 169.254.169.1:80 by default so it matches the
 IMDS bridge (vmbr_imds) and nftables DNAT of 169.254.169.254:80.
 Empty inventory_path falls back to Proxmox /etc/pve.
 .
 This package ships the vtpm-mds daemon, legacy aliases prox-mds and
 qemu-mds, a systemd unit, and a Proxmox-oriented default config. It is
 meant for hypervisors only. The guest-side enrollment client is packaged
 separately as devid-enroll and belongs in VM images, not on the host.
 Host swTPM PKI and the IMDS network are provided separately (Ansible
 roles proxmox-swtpm / proxmox-imds-network).

Package: devid-enroll
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: vtpm-mds (<< 0.2.0)
Replaces: vtpm-mds (<< 0.2.0)
Description: Guest DevID enrollment client for vtpm-mds
 devid-enroll runs inside a QEMU guest and enrolls the guest vTPM with the
 hypervisor metadata service reachable at 169.254.169.254, obtaining a TPM
 DevID/LDevID certificate for the guest identity.
 .
 It writes the SPIRE tpm_devid node attestor materials (DevID certificate,
 private and public key blobs) so a SPIRE agent in the guest can attest
 with its vTPM.
 .
 This package contains the client binary and its man page only. It ships
 no daemon, no systemd unit, and no IMDS listener, and it does not require
 the vtpm-mds package.
